<title>USA: DowElanco buys majority share of Mycogen.</title>
<headline>DowElanco buys majority share of Mycogen.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>DowElanco has bought a controlling share in Mycogen Corp in what sources say is a move to block a Monsanto Co bid for the agricultural-biotechnology concern, The Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>DowElanco, a pesticide venture formed by Dow Chemical Co, and Eli Lilly &amp; Co, lifted its stake in Mycogen to 51.8 percent from 47.3 percent by buying one million Mycogen shares from seed giant Pioneer Hi-Bred International Inc for $16.8 million, the report said.</p>
</text>
